To test a InfoServer 100 do this
Just like the VAX plug the cable into the MMJ port next to the serial
port
Just like the VAX it will count down. Since its not connected to your
network
you will get the >>>. Do a show device.
More then likely you will have either a RZ23/24 drive
check for this
BFLG D0000000
Halt 2
boot device dka100,dka200 (the 2 RDD42)
the RZ2X will be DKA0
If everything is okay then just type
>>>B dka0
If the drive has the Infoserver software installed it will come up.If
the Infoserver ask for a
password the default password is ESS (uppper or lower)
hope this helps
ps
I still use 5 InfoServers
phil



