SF200 and SF210 were DSSI storage arrays.  The SF200 came with RF72 1GB
series disks in arrays; the SF210 came with RF73 2GB disks in arrays.
Each could hold up to 6 SABBs (Storage Array Building Blocks), with
four identical drives per SABB, so the maximum capacity was 24GB for
the SF200, and 48GB for the SF210.

Each array could also contain up to two TF857 DLT seven cartridge tape
loader system.  It used DECtape III cartridges with 2.6GB capacity
each.



